# Example skill: one-line summary

This is a standard [Agent Skill](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) — the same
`SKILL.md` format works with Claude, Cursor, and other Agent Skills tools. The
harness injected this skill's *name* and *description* into the system prompt
(progressive disclosure, ~100 tokens). You are reading the full body because the
model called `read_skill("example-skill")` (or a file tool) to load it on demand.

## Instructions

When summarizing:

1. Read the user's text in full.
2. Produce **one sentence, 20 words or fewer**, capturing only the main point.
3. Prefix the answer with `Summary: `.
4. Do not add commentary, bullet points, or follow-up questions.

## Going further (L3)

Heavier skills can ship `scripts/` (run them with a shell tool), `references/`,
and `assets/` (read them with a file tool) alongside this `SKILL.md`. Scripts are
high-risk, so the relevant tool stays off until you enable it in `config.yaml`.

Delete this folder if you don't want the example — skills are just directories
under `skills/` (see `config.yaml` → `skills.dirs`).
